Day 18    Contamination
Day 19    Multi-stage protocols
Day 20    Full protocol design
Then we stop giving you artificial exercises and start giving you messy real-world problems.
That's when the skill becomes yours.
Your first fundamental rule
I want you to remember this one:
Never begin by asking, "What should I tell the AI?"
First ask:
"What state do I want the AI to produce, and what rules must govern how it gets there?"
That single change in thinking is enormous.
For an ordinary instruction:
TASK
 ↓
INSTRUCTION
 ↓
RESULT
For a strong instruction:
DESIRED STATE
 ↓
TASK DECOMPOSITION
 ↓
CONSTRAINTS
 ↓
EXECUTION RULES
 ↓
VERIFICATION
 ↓
RESULT
For a protocol:
QUESTION
 ↓
HYPOTHESIS
 ↓
CONTROLLED SYSTEM
 ↓
PROCEDURE
 ↓
MEASUREMENT
 ↓
VALIDITY
 ↓
INTERPRETATION
 ↓
DECISION
That's the skill set I'll teach you.
And yes — you can eventually become capable of creating instructions and protocols for things you've never seen before, because you'll be learning the underlying construction logic rather than copying my EXP-003 format.